  "releaseNotes": "1.2.4: a Kafka consumer can no longer stop reading silently. Offsets are committed in the background (stored only after the handler finishes) instead of synchronously after every message, so an unreachable group coordinator cannot block the loop. A watchdog rebuilds the Kafka client when the consumer has been out of its group for Auderz:Kafka:ConsumerStallSeconds (120), handlers are cancelled after ConsumerHandlerTimeoutSeconds (120) and dead-lettered, and the new kafka-consumer health check (tags ready, kafka) is served on /health/ready and on the new /health/kafka. No service code change.",
